// Colours of the cell grid overlay (WP2.4), the debug / planning view that
// the F1 panel's "Cell grid (4 m)" checkbox (or `--debug-grid`) switches on.
// Read by sf_render::cell_overlay. Colours are sRGB bytes (r, g, b).
//
// `types` names EVERY terrain type of terrain_types.ron (by name); a missing
// or unknown name is refused when the overlay is set up, so a new type cannot
// silently show up uncoloured. When WP2.3 (the minimap) lands its
// `minimap_colour` per type in terrain_types.ron, this table is meant to be
// replaced by that one: the overlay then only keeps the occupancy colours.
//
// What is drawn per 4 m cell (see docs/rules/cell_overlay.md):
//   open        the type colour, translucent (`fill_percent`)
//   impassable  the type colour with dark diagonal hatching: no ground class
//               (foot, wheeled, tracked) may enter the type
//   units       `units` colour, a disc in the cell: at least one unit's
//               position is in the cell (presentation only, the sim does
//               not track units per cell)
//   structure   `structure` colour, filled and outlined: the sim's
//               occupancy says a structure stands on the cell
(
    fill_percent: 35,
    types: {
        "grass": (96, 184, 72),
        "road": (200, 176, 120),
        "water": (48, 112, 224),
        "rock": (128, 120, 112),
        "ore": (232, 184, 32),
        "bridge": (176, 96, 40),
    },
    units: (40, 230, 230),
    structure: (230, 40, 120),
)
